I hope some of you nethack 'experts' out there can help me out,
because I'm not sure how to get out of my current stupid dilema. First
let me give you some background. I started playing a samaria so I
could be 'lawful' and be able to make holy water easily. Well, as luck
would have it I'm clear down to the castle level... and not a single
altar!

Inspite of this I'm having a great game. I was stumped for awhile
trying to get into the castle. I didn't have an instrument, or a wand
that could get through the door. I had a wand of cold and of fire and
so I thought I would try to blast my way around the moat. I first used
my wand of cold straight down, which froze the moat half way to the
outer border... cool. I went as far as I could, and then used the wand
of fire to clear out the rest of the moat below me. Unfortunatly the
bolt of fire bounced off of the border, and with a loud hissing sound
all the moat 'unfroze' and there I was, suspended above the castle
moat. I was invisible, and so I could actually see water right
underneath me.  Great... I couldn't move forward or backward without
falling in and drowning, I had assumed that once those little {
characters dissappeared they were gone, but not so. I finally ended up
reading a blessed scroll of teleportation and beaming myself up a few
levels.

Well, back up a few levels I run into a monster carrying, lo and
behold, a teleportation control ring. I put it on, jumped onto a level
teleport trap, and teleported to the level below the castle. I then
came up the back way, used a levitation potion I had found to get
across the trap doors, and went in to nab the wand of wishing. I had
to use another teleportation scroll to get back out of the castle.

OK, I used up my wishes (I actually had to wish for holy water! I had
a pile of unblessed water, but nothing to bless it with since there
were no altars.) I then jumped onto the level teleporter trap, and
beamed down to level 50 to confront the wizard. Well, I found him on
level 49... surrounded by a little mini-moat. Great, I had left my
wand of fire back on level 28. I wasn't sure how else to get around
that moat problem with what I had, but luckily I found another level
teleporter trap on that level. I thought I'd just pop up to level 28,
grab the wand, and be back. Well, I teleported up, got the wand... and
then realized that *all* level teleport traps had dissapeared! I guess
they go away once you go to hell and back. Now I had to figure out how
to get back down again. I found another leviation potion, blessed it,
and walked around the moat. I then dove down one of the trap doors to
the first level of hell. Unfortunately the floor is too hard to dig
into, and I can't figure out how to get down any further. I can go
back up to the castle level, but now I can't get back around the
moat. I have a wand of teleportation, but 'some mysterious force'
prevents me from using it. All I can do now is go from the right half
of the castle level to the first level of hell and back... I'm stuck.
Aaaaargh.... any ideas?  ... anybody?  I'd hate to come so far only to
get stuck with something so stupid. I mean I *saw* the wizard himself,
and now I can't go anywhere (sigh).

